0..77 Comment "// Freshness conditions on rules (Fernández and Gabbay, _Nominal rewriting_,"
78..155 Comment "// I&C 2007; Pitts, _Nominal Sets_, CUP 2013). A rule between terms closes on"
156..234 Comment "// a `where` clause, `where a # q`: the atom `a` stands outside the support of"
235..308 Comment "// the term `q` stands for. A rule whose variable moves into or out of an"
309..387 Comment "// abstraction states that atom fresh for it, or the description check refuses"
388..463 Comment "// the rule for capture (`pathological/desc/freshness.gandr`). The value of"
464..541 Comment "// `Theory` keeps each condition as a `Fresh` link after its rule. No port of"
542..617 Comment "// these theories takes an atom, so no term names one: the support of every"
618..695 Comment "// instance is empty and every condition holds. Where a port takes an atom, a"
696..738 Comment "// condition decides where its rule fires:"
739..777 Comment "// `model/desc/atom-occurrence.gandr`."
779..851 Comment "/// The π-calculus\'s structural congruence: the inert process, parallel"
852..921 Comment "/// composition and restriction, scope extrusion moving `q` under the"
922..1000 Comment "/// restriction fresh for its atom. The checker orients the law and the kernel"
1001..1025 Comment "/// replays the verdict."
